            .filter(existing -> today.equals(existing.getRegistrationDate()))
            .count();
    if (createdToday >= DAILY_LIMIT) {
        throw new OwnerDailyLimitReachedException(today);
    }
}
```
It counts all existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()`; at 100+ it throws. Supporting files:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/OwnerDailyLimitReachedException.java` — carries the date; message `"Daily owner creation limit reached for: " + date`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/OwnerDailyLimitReachedExceptionHandler.java` — responds `429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` with the message as body.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.OwnerDailyLimitReachedException.yml` — registers that handler.

### 5. Owner entity and DTOs
Entity: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`. Relevant columns (lines 55-68): `registrationDate` (LocalDate, `registration_date` DATE), `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, `householdId`, `namesakeCount`, plus address/city/telephone/email. Standard getters/setters follow.

DTOs are **generated from OpenAPI** at build time (no `.java` source on disk; `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto`/`OwnerPageDto` are referenced but not present under `src`). The source of truth is `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`:
- `OwnerFields` schema (line 1991) — editable input fields. `registrationDate` at lines 2046-2053 (`format: date`, "When omitted on creation it defaults to the server's current date"). Also `sharesHousehold` (2054-2061). Required: firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone.
- `Owner` schema (line 2068) — `allOf` OwnerFields plus read-only derived fields: `customerCode` (2095), `membershipNumber` (2106-2114, documents the `<customerCode>-M<YY>` / last-two-digits-of-registrationDate-year rule), `householdId` (2115), `namesakeCount` (2124), `membershipTier` (2135), `locality` (2143).

Mapper: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` (full content, 74 lines). `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (line 57-59, ignores id and pets) is what BuildOwner calls — registrationDate maps straight through by name. `toOwnerDto` adds derived `membershipTier` (SILVER if namesakeCount==0 and email present, else BRONZE), `locality`, `displayName`, `initials`.

Other pipeline functions (full contents read):
- `SaveOwner.java` (13 lines) — `ownerRepository.save(owner)`.
- `CountOwnerNamesakes.java` (33 lines) — sets `namesakeCount` from case-insensitive first+last name matches among existing owners (before save, so self not counted).
- `RespondWithOwnerCreated.java` (19 lines) — maps to OwnerDto, returns `201 Created` with Location `/api/owners/{id}`.
- `ValidateOwnerFields.java` (79 lines) — first step; binds `@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (the only step that reads the body), validates/normalizes fields, republishes via `Out<OwnerFieldsDto>`. Does **not** touch registrationDate.

### 6. Tests related to owner creation / registration date / membership / daily limit
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` (20 lines) — one `@Test`:
```java
@Test
void coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay() throws Exception {
    int id = createOwnerOk(ownerNode());
    DayOfWeek dow = LocalDate.parse(fetchOwner(id).get("registrationDate").asText()).getDayOfWeek();
    assertTrue(dow != DayOfWeek.SATURDAY && dow != DayOfWeek.SUNDAY, dow.toString());
}
```
It creates an owner with no registrationDate and asserts the defaulted date is never a weekend.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` (322 lines) — the harness (MockMvc-based). Relevant helpers:
- `createOwner` / `createOwnerOk` (lines 155-162) POST `/api/owners`; `fetchOwner` (200), `getOwner`, `extractId`.
- `ownerNode()` (117-125) builds a valid owner with no registrationDate; `today()` (110-112).
- `createMany(n)` (183-187) and `fillCity(city,n)` (173-179) — drive the per-day limit and per-city capacity rules.
- `toBusinessDay(LocalDate)` (267-274) rolls weekends and `HOLIDAYS` (240-242, five pinned 2026 dates) forward — the expected business-day algorithm.
- Also `AuditLogCapture.java` in the same package.

## Important discrepancy worth noting
The test harness encodes a **business-day roll** for the default registration date: `AcceptanceTest.coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay` asserts the default is never Sat/Sun, and `AcceptanceBase.toBusinessDay` (plus a `HOLIDAYS` set) rolls weekends/holidays forward to the next business day. But production `BuildOwner.java` defaults with a plain `LocalDate.now()` and performs **no** weekend/holiday adjustment. A `grep` across `src/main` for `DayOfWeek|SATURDAY|SUNDAY|businessDay|weekend|plusDays` returned nothing — the business-day roll is not implemented in the pipeline. If the current server date falls on a weekend/holiday, `coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay` would fail. This looks like a feature expected by the tests/spec but missing from `BuildOwner`.

